      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Light: NC State says partial shade and very low light tolerated, Penn State and Clemson say bright indirect; the preferred level is stored. Size: sources give leaf length (up to 4 ft) but no spread, so size stays unknown. Severity 1 is the agent's grading of 'low' (NC State). Interval: NC State 'allow soil to dry between waterings' (spring and autumn; 'in winter only water every one to two months'); Missouri Botanical Garden 'water regularly during growing season, significantly reduced watering fall to late winter'. Neither gives days; 'dry between waterings' in a 13 cm pot takes about two weeks, so 14. The winter wording suggests a rest factor above the 1.6 stored (review). Pot and season: 13 cm pot, bright indirect light, room temperature, growing season. Dry and wet tolerance days: no source gives days, left as before (from_knowledge_verify)."
      },
